CM TM-WHP-NEC-011
CM Roll-up wire version — 5.6m with inline LC traps, 10m active
CM ---------------------------------------------------------------
CM This model represents the roll-up wire dipole/vertical variant:
CM a full 5.6m wire with series LC traps at four positions to create
CM band-specific resonant sections. Active model: 10m (28.0-29.7 MHz)
CM
CM TRAP THEORY AND OPERATION:
CM Each trap is a parallel LC circuit (or series notch) placed inline.
CM At the trap's resonant frequency, impedance is very high (parallel
CM resonance), electrically isolating the wire beyond that point.
CM Below trap frequency, trap is inductive (adds loading effect).
CM
CM For a SERIES-mode trap model in NEC-2 (LD 0 type):
CM   The trap resonant impedance is approximated as series R+jX.
CM   At resonance the parallel tank is high-Z; we model the OFF-resonance
CM   effect (inductive below fc) as added series reactance.
CM   This is an approximation; a full trap model requires two-port network.
CM
CM TRAP POSITIONS AND PARAMETERS (from base, along wire):
CM   10m trap:  segment ~18 (at z~2.55m): fc=28.5 MHz, L=0.32uH, C=97pF
CM              Series model at 28.5 MHz: R~12 ohm, XL~57 ohm
CM   12m trap:  segment ~21 (at z~2.92m): fc=24.9 MHz, L=0.42uH, C=98pF
CM              Series model at 24.9 MHz: R~10 ohm, XL~66 ohm
CM   15m trap:  segment ~24 (at z~3.43m): fc=21.2 MHz, L=0.58uH, C=97pF
CM              Series model at 21.2 MHz: R~ 8 ohm, XL~77 ohm
CM   17m trap:  segment ~28 (at z~4.01m): fc=18.1 MHz, L=0.81uH, C=96pF
CM              Series model at 18.1 MHz: R~ 7 ohm, XL~92 ohm
CM
CM BAND OPERATION SUMMARY:
CM   10m (28-29.7 MHz): only 10m trap high-Z; active section = 0-2.55m
CM      12m/15m/17m traps below resonance — inductive, add loading
CM      At 28.5 MHz: 10m trap isolates; wire beyond is inactive
CM   12m (24.9 MHz): 10m trap is capacitive (below fc); passes current
CM      12m trap at z=2.92m goes high-Z; active section = 0-2.92m
CM   15m (21.2 MHz): active section = 0-3.43m (below all traps above)
CM   17m (18.1 MHz): active section = 0-4.01m
CM   20m+ (below 18.1 MHz): all traps pass current; full wire active
CM      Use base loading coil for 30m, 40m, 80m, 160m resonance
CM
CM BASE LOADING COIL (for 20m and below):
CM   20m: wire slightly long at 5.6m; capacitive trimmer or small L
CM   30m: L=2.477uH, XL=157.6 ohm, R=0.493 ohm (LD at seg 1)
CM   40m: L=7.85uH, XL=353 ohm, R=1.14 ohm (LD at seg 1)
CM   80m: L=35.5uH, XL=835 ohm, R=2.98 ohm (LD at seg 1)
CM   160m: L=144.6uH, XL=1725 ohm, R=6.90 ohm (LD at seg 1)
CM
CM ACTIVE MODEL: 10m band (28.0-29.7 MHz)
CM   Base loading: none (no LD at seg 1 for 10m)
CM   10m trap at seg 18: R=12, X=57 (series RL approximation)
CM   12m trap at seg 21: R=10, X=66
CM   15m trap at seg 24: R=8, X=77
CM   17m trap at seg 28: R=7, X=92
CM
CM Wire geometry:
CM   GW 1: main wire, 40 segs, z=0.005 to z=5.605, radius=0.006m
CM   GW 2-5: 4 radials at z=0.005, length=5.6m
CM
CM Segment mapping (40 segs over 5.6m = 0.14m/seg):
CM   z=2.55m -> seg = 2.55/0.14 = 18.2 -> use seg 18
CM   z=2.92m -> seg = 2.92/0.14 = 20.9 -> use seg 21
CM   z=3.43m -> seg = 3.43/0.14 = 24.5 -> use seg 25
CM   z=4.01m -> seg = 4.01/0.14 = 28.6 -> use seg 29
CM
CM Ground: real average soil (GN 2), sigma=0.005 S/m, epsilon_r=13
CM Feed: voltage source EX 0 on segment 1 of GW1
CE
GW 1 40  0.0 0.0 0.005  0.0 0.0 5.605  0.006
GW 2 20  0.0 0.0 0.005  5.6 0.0 0.005  0.006
GW 3 20  0.0 0.0 0.005 -5.6 0.0 0.005  0.006
GW 4 20  0.0 0.0 0.005  0.0 5.6 0.005  0.006
GW 5 20  0.0 0.0 0.005  0.0 -5.6 0.005  0.006
GE 1
GN 2 0 0 0  13 0.005
CM 10m trap at segment 18 (z~2.52m): series R+jX approx at 28.5 MHz
LD 0 1 18 18  12.0 57.0
CM 12m trap at segment 21 (z~2.94m): series R+jX approx at 24.9 MHz
LD 0 1 21 21  10.0 66.0
CM 15m trap at segment 25 (z~3.50m): series R+jX approx at 21.2 MHz
LD 0 1 25 25  8.0 77.0
CM 17m trap at segment 29 (z~4.06m): series R+jX approx at 18.1 MHz
LD 0 1 29 29  7.0 92.0
EX 0 1 1 0  1 0
FR 0 9 0 0  28.000 0.213
RP 0 37 73 1000  0 0 5 5
EN
